            <ArticleTitle>Pulmonary endometriosis mimicking an acute abdomen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>865-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of pulmonary endometriosis is reported, to illustrate the classic catamenial symptoms of the disease. The patient also developed symptoms and signs suggesting a perforated abdominal viscus; laparotomy was normal and the features may have resulted from a previously unreported effect of diaphragmatic endometrial foci.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
